    "text": "Energy: each appliance's watts × quantity × hours a day (inverter ACs at their average draw), added up = 16.2 units a day; ÷ 4 units per kW of panels a day for your city = 4.06 kW. Power: 5,540 W running load ÷ 0.78 performance ratio = 7.1 kW, so the panels can carry everything at Zuhr or at the shop's midday peak. The larger, 7.1 kW, needs 13 panels of 585 W = 7.61 kW, about 913 units a month. Inverter = 5,540 W × 1.25 = 6.93 kW, with a surge rating of at least 7,340 W."
